# Deny-by-default: everything is excluded from the VSIX unless explicitly
# allowlisted below via `!` negation. Replaces a denylist that grew
# reactively and kept missing new file types - dev tooling added since
# (test/, vitest.config.*, eslint.config.mjs, scripts/release.js) was never
# added to the old denylist and was shipping in the VSIX unnoticed.
#
# vsce's `!` matching is NOT git's last-pattern-wins: reading
# node_modules/@vscode/vsce/out/package.js's collectFiles(), it splits this
# file into a plain-pattern list and a `!`-prefixed list, then keeps a file
# if it *either* misses every plain pattern *or* matches any `!` pattern -
# a `!` match always wins, regardless of pattern order or a later, more
# specific plain pattern that might also match. Concretely: a broad
# `!pets/*/spritesheet*.png` would have unignored cat-stack's unused/stray
# spritesheet.png right along with flux-red's real one, and no later deny
# line could claw it back. So every allow rule below is written as narrow as
# the actual runtime read it corresponds to (see src/pets.ts, src/webview.ts)
# rather than a convenient shared wildcard. (Also verified empirically with
# `npx vsce ls` before settling on this.)
**

!LICENSE
!out/**/*.js
!media/**

# pets/: allow only the exact files src/pets.ts and src/webview.ts read at
# runtime for each pet - the manifest, its spritesheet (flux-red's manifest
# is the one pet that points at a .png; every other pet points at .webp),
# and the nonstandard-seamless variant's webp+json when present. Everything
# else in a pet's folder is sprite-pipeline QA/scratch (contact sheets,
# validation/motion/alignment reports, preview gifs, pets/_runs/, backups,
# the unused nonstandard-fluid variant, cat-stack's stray duplicate
# spritesheet.png) and stays excluded by the blanket deny above since
# nothing here matches it.
!pets/*/pet.json
!pets/*/spritesheet.webp
!pets/flux-red/spritesheet.png
!pets/*/nonstandard-seamless/spritesheet-seamless.webp
!pets/*/nonstandard-seamless/spritesheet-seamless.json
